{"id": "EUVD-2026-82018", "enisaUuid": "7c498b89-c860-3e85-95e6-a481270a5012", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: unlink TWT flow if the MCU rejects the agreement\n\nThe flow is added to dev->twt_list before sending the agreement to the\nfirmware, but the error path leaves it linked while flowid_mask is\nnever set. The flow slot can then be reused and memset while still on\nthe list, corrupting twt_list, and station removal leaves a dangling\nentry behind that mt7915_mac_twt_sched_list_add() later walks.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:13", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c09d1b15ed2dc49060303b16a296b7b8b7794cbe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bd5c4ed2b9045faf83315c54cd37a9b7c71b5c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cabe239e95b4eebf5b6c3654087b66ff9425bc7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bce0f1280c94af8314f895f404629da09f0788c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/beaa42b875965dbc3e80e46970e0bfa60a94c2db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16a04441eab0dcd4d7126a6f66b370adbf28f96d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90357", "GHSA-9px9-hrqm-cp96"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b664cdf-ded0-39b8-b50b-fc45259271af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3782b69d03e714b8ff98b84c7426d8cef0e64d7c <16a04441eab0dcd4d7126a6f66b370adbf28f96d"}, {"id": "0c8e1d94-fa4a-3f95-9407-23defcff32bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "10b4f35f-6e49-3ce6-af74-2be2d2f9a5f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "42622f17-8444-37a3-a235-3053e391599e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id"